ng capabilities and  there was no clear indication that there  could ever be  a flying titan but that all changed once  we got to chapter 133  of the manga but before we talk about  that we need to talk about falco grice  and his jaw titan power when we first  meet him  falco is a marlin warrior candidate who  is hoping to be chosen to succeed reiner  as the next armored titan but all of his  plans change when he is abducted along  with gabby  and taken to the island of paradise  while on parodies  falco accidentally ingests some of the  wine that was  tainted with zeke's spinal fluid and so  once  zeke eventually uses his scream to  transform a bunch of the aldians on the  island into pure titans  falco is transformed as well as a pure  titan  falco has no control of his actions and  during the course of the subsequent  battle  falco's pure titan ends up eating porco  galliard which gives falco the power of  the jaw titan  falco is then able to return to his  human form  and the first time he transforms into  his new jaw titan form  it is clear that his jaw titan has some  distinct  bird-like features including talons and  an  outer jaw that resembles a beak at first  i didn't think that these bird-like  features had  any significant meaning all of the jaw  titans that we've seen thus far have  been very unique and very  different from each other so i thought  that falco's  titan was probably just unique to him  and i thought that his appearance was a  nod to the name  falco which means falcon in latin  but in chapter 133  falco says something that is extremely  interesting and something that ends up  being  extremely important falco says that he  had a vivid dream that felt  more like a real memory only not his  memory it appeared to be a memory that  falco inherited from zeke  through zeke's spinal fluid in this  dream  or memory falco sees himself flying  above the clouds and he concludes that  these are the memories of a previous  beast titan shifter now zeke's beast  titan is obviously an  ape but falco believes that in the past  the beast titan shifters  looked very different they weren't all  ape-like  some were based on completely different  beasts altogether  and falco believes that some beast  titans actually had wings  and were able to fly at this point falco  is convinced that his jaw titan has to  some extent  inherited the abilities of the previous  beast titans  through zeke's spinal fluid and this  leads falco to conclude that his  jaw titan has the potential to gain the  ability to fly  just like some of the previous beast  titans in the video that i made  on chapter 133 in particular i  speculated that falco would in fact  gain the ability to fly and i said that  i thought that he and annie would be  able to join the main battle against  aaron by flying up to him  using falco's flying jaw titan and  this is exactly what ended up happening  in chapter 135.  that's when we see annie and gabby ride  atop of falco's jaw titan to rescue  their allies from the new titan shifters  that emir fritz  sent after them in this new flying titan  form  falco's jaw titan has fully developed  wings  and it is able to easily carry at least  seven people on  its back while flying and this is how  the old  fan theory about a flying titan shifter  a theory that most fans abandoned after  all nine shifters were introduced and  none of them could fly  actually came true in chapter 135  and it wasn't the beast titan shifter  who gained the ability to fly by  becoming a flying  beast instead it was the jaw titan who  unlocked the ability to fly  due to falco's direct connection to the  beast titan shifter  through zeke's spinal fluid man this is  definitely not something that i expected  would happen before  falco inherited the jaw titan powers i  definitely wouldn't have thought that  the jaw titan out of all the titans  would be the one to unlock  the ability to fly but there you have it  fun fact way back in april of 2017 the  attack on titan's season 2 opening  clearly hinted at the fact that the  beast titan shifter can potentially take  on  many different beast forms we clearly  see the beast  titan running alongside a bunch of other  beasts including a crocodile  but more on the crocodile later in terms  of falco's jaw titan we know that he is  very strong fast and  agile just like the other jaw titans  but as of the making of this video we  still haven't seen his flying titan form  in action we've seen him fly and carry  his allies on his back  but we haven't seen him actually trying  to engage in combat  at least not yet but still the fact that  this titan can fly  is an absolutely huge deal this is a  game-changing ability that allowed annie  and falco to rejoin the main battle  after they had initially split up from  the rest of their comrades  and it is also an ability that will turn  out to be extremely important in the  fight against aaron's  absolutely gigantic new titan form  i mean falco's flying titan was already  able to save the lives of multiple  people  so you better believe that this power is  going to continue being useful during  the final  epic showdown and that is what we know  about falco's titan thus far  and that is how a jaw titan was able to  gain the ability to  fly i got a ton of questions about this  in the comments to my previous attack on  titan videos  so i wanted to answer all of those  questions here at least based on the  information that we have so far  on top of that i also got a lot of  questions about the new titan shifters  that appeared in chapter 135  i am talking about the shifters that  attacked the anti-aaron alliance as they  climbed aaron's gigantic titan in an  attempt to reach the physical bodies of  aaron and zeke these  are definitely titan shifters they are  not pure titans  and although many of them are new to us  because we've never seen them before  in reality they are old titan shifters  more specifically their previous titan  shifters that existed at some point  between the death of emir fritz  and the present time these former  shifters were resurrected by emir fritz  and sent to attack  the anti-aaron alliance in an effort to  protect aaron from harm  among these former titan shifters we see  some titans that we can recognize  including the former jaw titan rest in  peace porco  the former warhammer titan and the  former colossal titan  but we also see shifters that we've  never seen before  including a beast titan who looks like a  crocodile  and we also see what appeared to be  previous armored titans  warhammer titans jaw titans and so on  seeing all of these former titans  attacking some of our favorite  characters was both  kinda cool and absolutely terrifying  and to be honest i would love to know  more about all of these titan shifters  and their holders but will we ever learn  more about these former titans  probably not much since there is just so  much stuff going on in the main story of  attack on titan but  with that said we definitely will learn  more about  falco's new flying titan and i'm really  looking forward to that  now let me know what you guys think did  you like the flying titan twist  and were you expecting it did you think  that the twist made sense  in terms of the story the whole zeke  spinal fluid connection  or did you maybe think that it kind of  came out of nowhere  also do levi mikasa armin and the others  stand a chance against  aaron even with falco's flying titan  is there any way to defeat all those  overpowered  former titan shifters not to mention  aaron's gigantic  titan and finally how will this  incredible story  ultimately end don't forget to share  your thoughts  down in the comments below huge thank  you to  omarvin for letting me feature some of  his amazing attack on titan fan art  in my videos including this fan art of  falco's jaw  titan definitely check him out and show  him some love  the link to his twitter is down in the  description  and 